        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Israel strikes Beirut and southern Lebanon despite truce On the ground Issued on: 07/05/2026 - 18:08 Israel pummelled southern Lebanon on Thursday, state media and AFP correspondents said, a day after it targeted a Hezbollah commander in its first strike on Beirut's southern suburbs since a truce sought to end weeks of fighting. The Israeli army said Thursday that the strike on the southern suburbs killed \"the Commander of Hezbollah's 'Radwan Force' Unit\", an elite unit within the Iran-backed armed group Hezbollah. FRANCE 24's Renée Davis reports from Beirut, Lebanon. Brazil’s Lula to discuss fighting organized crime, tariffs in Trump meeting 07/05/2026 Hantavirus: Video of first death reported by crew captain 07/05/2026 Travel Russian attacks kill 27 before deadline for ceasefire proposed by Kyiv 07/05/2026 World Cup 2026: FIFA under fire for ticket prices 07/05/2026 Israel says it killed Hezbollah commander in first strike on Beirut since ceasefire 07/05/2026 Israel's war priorities sidelined as Trump pushes toward a limited deal with Iran 07/05/2026 French aircraft carrier pre-positions for possible Hormuz mission 07/05/2026 War in the Middle East: Satellite imagery reveal scale of damage to US bases in Gulf 07/05/2026 Starmer under pressure: 'Many Labour MPs can’t see UK PM leading them into next general election' 07/05/2026 UK"
